builder_directive_outside_datasource: in an ordinary .ssl script every
builder directive, in any case, is an error (a script containing one does
not compile), and unknown_keyword does not also fire on it. Both an
uppercase and a lowercase directive are here; the lowercase one must not
pick up a second, case-related finding instead.
-- input.ssl --
:DSN := DATABASE;
:nullasblank := true;
:DECLARE aRows;
aRows := RunDS("Stock.ByBin", {"A1"});
:RETURN aRows;
-- format --
:DSN := DATABASE;
:NULLASBLANK := true;
:DECLARE aRows;

aRows := RunDS("Stock.ByBin", {"A1"});

:RETURN aRows;
-- diagnostics --
1:1-1:5 error builder_directive_outside_datasource: ':DSN' is a data source builder directive and is valid only in a data source file
2:1-2:13 error builder_directive_outside_datasource: ':nullasblank' is a data source builder directive and is valid only in a data source file
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
1:1-1:5 error builder_directive_outside_datasource: ':DSN' is a data source builder directive and is valid only in a data source file
1:9-1:17 warning undeclared_variable: Variable 'DATABASE' is not declared
2:1-2:13 error builder_directive_outside_datasource: ':nullasblank' is a data source builder directive and is valid only in a data source file
2:17-2:21 warning undeclared_variable: Variable 'true' is not declared
